# What never enters the image build context.
#
# docker/Dockerfile copies the repository with `COPY . .`, so anything not
# listed here is sent to the daemon and can end up in a layer. Three things
# must never be: secrets, signed evidence, and the host's own build output.

# Secrets. The template is fine; a real .env is not.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Signed handover evidence and issue photos. Personal data, and the runtime
# mounts its own volume at /app/storage regardless.
storage/
storage-e2e/

# Host build output and caches. The image builds its own.
.next/
.next-e2e/
node_modules/
coverage/
playwright-report/
test-results/
*.tsbuildinfo

# Development tooling and history.
.git/
.github/
.vscode/
.idea/
*.log
npm-debug.log*

# Tests are not shipped.
tests/
playwright.config.ts
vitest.config.mts

# Documentation is read from the repository, not from the container.
docs/
*.md
!README.md
